        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>In a blast furnace, iron is extracted from haematite ($Fe_2O_3$) by reducing it with carbon monoxide ($CO$), which is produced from the reaction of coke (carbon) with oxygen. The $CO$ reduces the iron oxide to molten iron.</p>",
